---
title: Design class diagram 1 of 8 - users, leads and cases (Strategies.Api/Data/Models)
---
classDiagram
    direction TB

    class User {
        <<entity>>
        +Id: Guid «PK»
        +FullName: string
        +Email: string
        +PasswordHash: string
        +Role: UserRole
        +IsActive: bool = true
        +EmailConfirmed: bool = false
        +CreatedAt: DateTime = UtcNow
    }
    class Lead {
        <<entity>>
        +Id: Guid «PK»
        +ReviewedById: Guid? «FK User»
        +VisaCategoryId: Guid? «FK VisaCategory»
        +FullName: string
        +Email: string
        +ImmigrationStatus: ImmigrationStatus
        +NeedsAssistance: bool
        +DesiredStartDate: DateTime
        +TriageStatus: TriageStatus
        +TriageReason: string?
        +SubmittedAt: DateTime = UtcNow
    }
    class Case {
        <<entity>>
        +Id: Guid «PK»
        +LeadId: Guid? «FK Lead»
        +ClientId: Guid «FK User»
        +ConsultantId: Guid? «FK User»
        +VisaCategoryId: Guid «FK VisaCategory»
        +Stage: CaseStage
        +IsArchived: bool = false
        +CreatedAt: DateTime = UtcNow
        +UpdatedAt: DateTime = UtcNow
    }
    class VisaCategory {
        <<entity>>
        +Id: Guid «PK»
        +Name: string
        +Description: string?
        +IsActive: bool = true
    }

    User "1" <-- "0..*" Case : client
    User "0..1" <-- "0..*" Case : consultant
    Lead "0..1" <-- "0..*" Case : converted from
    VisaCategory "1" <-- "0..*" Case
    User "0..1" <-- "0..*" Lead : reviewer
    VisaCategory "0..1" <-- "0..*" Lead

    note "Entities are EF Core classes with public properties only:<br>they declare no methods. Behaviour is in the controllers<br>and services (diagrams 5 to 8).<br>Case to client User and to VisaCategory: Restrict.<br>Optional links (Guid?): SetNull.<br>The classes hold foreign key ids, no navigation properties;<br>ApplicationDbContext.OnModelCreating configures the links."
